# <type>(<scope>): <summary>

# The subject is ONE line, 20 characters or fewer, no trailing period.
#   feat: 新增标签            <- 14 characters of summary left
#   feat(view): 加标签        <- 8 left; scopes are expensive at this budget
# A blank line starts the body, which says WHY, in at most 2 lines of 20.
# If the subject already says it, delete everything below this one.
#
# types:  feat fix docs test refactor perf build ci chore revert style
# scopes: view routing host client schema profile test docs
#
# Leave one blank line before any trailer git understands
# (Closes #12, Refs: …, Co-authored-by: …).
#
# Attribution lines ("Generated with …", "🤖", AI co-author addresses) are
# rejected: the message describes the change, not the tool that typed it.
#
# Lines starting with "#" are dropped by git. Set this file as the default:
#   git config commit.template .gitmessage
